# Endless Library: project context for every agent

This file is loaded by every agent (including subagents). Read it first. It describes the project, the rules and the
commands. When a rule here conflicts with a request, stop and ask the owner.

## What the project is

Endless Library is a learning project: a library with a REST API (FastAPI + SQLAlchemy 2 + PostgreSQL), a React + Vite +
TypeScript website, Redis cache, Docker and Kubernetes (kind), Prometheus and Grafana. Its main purpose is to practise and
demonstrate testing on every level. The repository is **public**: https://github.com/arsbatyrov/endless-library

## Language policy

- Chat with the owner: **Russian**.
- Documentation, tickets, bug reports, PR descriptions, ADRs, review comments: **English**.
- New code comments: English. Existing Russian comments and docstrings are left as they are unless the ticket says otherwise.
- User interface texts are bilingual (ru and en) in `frontend/src/i18n.ts`; both dictionaries must have every key.

## Layout

| Path | Contents |
|---|---|
| `app/` | FastAPI application (routers, services, models, schemas, cache, metrics, logging) |
| `migrations/` | Alembic migrations (single chain; `alembic check` must be clean) |
| `frontend/` | React website (`src/`), nginx config, Dockerfile |
| `tests/unit`, `tests/api`, `tests/db`, `tests/migrations`, `tests/concurrency` | Backend tests (run by default) |
| `tests/contract` | Schemathesis + OpenAPI snapshot (marker `contract`) |
| `tests/ui` | Playwright UI tests (marker `ui`) |
| `tests/smoke` | Tests of the deployed cluster (marker `smoke`) |
| `k8s/` | kind config, manifests, ingress, monitoring, `deploy.sh` |
| `docs/` | Documentation (this kit lives in `docs/agent-team/`) |

## Commands (Windows, PowerShell; the virtual environment is `.venv`)

```powershell
.\.venv\Scripts\python.exe -m pytest --no-cov -q            # default suite (unit, api, db, migrations, concurrency)
.\.venv\Scripts\python.exe -m pytest tests/unit --no-cov -q  # one folder
.\.venv\Scripts\python.exe -m pytest -m ui --no-cov -q       # UI tests (starts its own servers on 8100 and 5180)
.\.venv\Scripts\python.exe -m pytest tests/contract -m contract --no-cov -q
.\.venv\Scripts\python.exe -m pytest tests/smoke -m smoke --no-cov -q   # needs the cluster
.\.venv\Scripts\ruff.exe check . ; .\.venv\Scripts\ruff.exe format .
cd frontend ; npm run build                                  # type check and build
bash k8s/deploy.sh                                           # (re)deploy to the local cluster (Git Bash)
```

The default `pytest` run needs PostgreSQL and Redis (`docker compose up -d db redis`) and enforces 95% coverage.
Tests use the databases `library_test`, `library_e2e_test`, `library_migrations_test` and Redis database 15.

## Environment facts

| Thing | Value |
|---|---|
| The website (cluster) | http://127.0.0.1:8080 , API under `/api` , Swagger at `/api/docs` |
| Grafana | http://grafana.localhost:8080 (dashboard "Endless Library") |
| Cluster / context / namespace | `endless-library` / `kind-endless-library` / `endless-library` |
| Docker Compose project | `endless-library` (containers `endless-library-db-1`, `endless-library-redis-1`) |
| Dev servers of the owner | API 8000, Vite 5173: **never start your own servers there**; use 8765, 8100, 5180 |
| Working database | `library` (the owner's data, 50 books): **never read-write it from tests or experiments** |
| Compose data volume | `library_pgdata` (pinned by name; do not remove) |

## Hard rules (never break)

1. Do not touch the working database `library`, the owner's other containers, `.env`, or the `.claude/settings.local.json` file.
2. No force-push, no pushes to `main`. Work on a branch: `feat/...`, `fix/...`, `docs/...`, `chore/...`.
3. **Never merge a PR, close or create issues, change repository or project settings, create secrets, or deploy** without the
   owner's explicit approval in the current session (the orchestrator skills define the exact gates).
4. The repository is public: no secrets, tokens, passwords or personal data in code, tickets, logs, tests or test data.
5. Packages and Docker images are installed by the owner. If a ticket needs a new dependency, say so and stop; do not work around a denied install.
6. If acceptance criteria are unclear or contradictory, **stop and ask**; do not guess.

## Conventions

- Tests live next to their level (see Layout). Every test is linked to a requirement ID when the ticket has one. New tests
  must be able to fail: before you finish, break the code on purpose once and confirm the test goes red (mutation check).
- API changes update the OpenAPI snapshot deliberately: `UPDATE_OPENAPI_SNAPSHOT=1 pytest tests/contract/test_openapi_snapshot.py -m contract --no-cov`.
- Server error messages (`detail` of 404/409/422 responses) are shown by the UI as they are and are not translated.
- Frontend: every user-visible string goes through `i18n.ts`; elements that tests use have `data-testid`.
- Python 3.12, ruff is the only linter/formatter; CI runs seven required checks (Lint, Tests, Frontend, UI tests, Docker images,
  Contract tests, Kubernetes smoke tests). A PR is ready only when all are green.
- Commit messages and PR descriptions follow the attribution instructions provided by the harness. PR descriptions are English.
- Windows notes: PowerShell 5.1 has no `&&`; `.ps1` files must be ASCII-only; in Git Bash write `gh api` endpoints without a
  leading slash; create files with the Write tool rather than long shell heredocs; always set connection timeouts.

## Tickets and the board

- Tickets are GitHub issues in this repository, created from `.github/ISSUE_TEMPLATE/feature.yml` (feature) and a bug
  template (see `docs/agent-team/process/bug-triage.md` once active). Labels: type (`feature`, `bug`, `task`, `test`),
  priority (`priority:critical|high|mid|low`: for bugs set by the tester, for features by the owner), area (`area:api|web|android|infra|ci`).
- The project board "Endless Library" (https://github.com/users/arsbatyrov/projects/1) holds the ticket **Status**, which is
  the handoff signal between roles. See `docs/agent-team/process/agent-workflow.md`.
- Definition of Ready and Definition of Done are in the feature template. A ticket is not Ready without Given/When/Then criteria.

## How to report

Be brief and factual: what you did, what you verified (command and result), what is left, what you need from the owner.
Never claim a test passed without running it. If a step failed or was skipped, say so.
